<title>ROMANIA: Romania June net average wage up 2.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Romania June net average wage up 2.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's June average monthly net wage rose 2.3 percent, identical to a rise in June inflation, National Statistics Board (CNS) data showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p> ROMANIAN AVERAGE WAGES  JUNE 97     MAY 97    JUNE 96</p>
<p> monthly change	     +2.3	  -4.1	 +0.2</p>
<p> yr/yr change		+97.5	 +93.4	+43.4</p>
<p> wage in ROL	     580,978     567,647     294,148</p>
<p>NOTE: The CNS said purchasing power remained flat last month from May but was down 28.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>June's purchasing power was 49.7 percent of the 1990 level.</p>
<p>Employees in the banking sector had the highest net wage of 1.19 million lei on average in June. Workers in the tourism industry had the lowest pay of 408,282 lei ($56.62).</p>
<p>Romania employed 5.5 million people at end-June, 28,100 less than the previous month.</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264 ($ = 7210 Romanian Lei)</p>
</text>
